    stepID: Day2_GridBrief
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Morning! I started trying to draw a grid after yesterday's SFML setup, but I am not sure how to organize the tiles. Could you talk me through how you would approach it? I'd like to understand it before we get to ship placement.
    displayDuration: 15.9
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_GridRequirements
    alternateNextStepID: 
    awardSkillKey: 
    narrativeEventKey: 
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge: {fileID: 0}
  - message:
      messageId: a0d23ed7764f40ceb1df0c0ec4df5c1e
      contactKey: friend
      contactName: Friend
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
      text: 
      replies: []
      waitForReply: 0
    stepID: Day2_GridRequirements
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: For my first attempt, I used eight rows, eight columns, forty-pixel cells, and an origin of one hundred, eighty. Would you keep those values together somewhere? I am worried I will have to rewrite the positions if the size changes.
    displayDuration: 14.8
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_ChooseApproach
    alternateNextStepID: 
    awardSkillKey: 
    narrativeEventKey: 
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge: {fileID: 0}
  - message:
      messageId: d735f0d417dc4499a5d384346f18b574
      contactKey: friend
      contactName: Friend
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
      text: 
      replies: []
      waitForReply: 0
    stepID: Day2_ChooseApproach
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Where would you start? Could you explain your reasoning so I can follow along?
    displayDuration: 5.2
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: Let us draw one tile first and make sure we understand its position before duplicating it.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Use row and column numbers to position each tile, instead of choosing every position by hand.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Define the origin, cell size, rows, and columns once, then generate the tiles with nested loops.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Use shared settings and nested loops, then verify the origin, last cell, and loop bounds before we call it done.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Separate grid configuration from drawing, generate from one position rule, and verify both square and rectangular dimensions.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: I will place the first few squares by eye and copy them until it resembles a grid.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Copy the first row, move each copy down forty pixels, and adjust anything that looks wrong.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Use two short loops with eight and forty written directly into them. We can expose settings later.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Make a quick drawing helper, keep the fixed eight-by-eight settings, and check the screenshot.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Use a compact loop with adjustable row and column counts. Skip the edge-case tests so we can demo immediately.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: We got SFML running yesterday. Let us keep using that setup while I review the grid.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: We already have yesterday's CLion project. Let us keep that environment consistent while I look over the implementation.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: You configured SFML through CMakeLists.txt yesterday. Keep that setup in place while I review how the grid should fit into it.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: Yesterday you set SFML_DIR for the downloaded library. We can preserve that configuration while I decide how to organize the grid.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: You kept SFML under external/ and connected it through CMake yesterday. Let us retain that environment while I review the drawing approach.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
