  - message:
      messageId: 3c7e5baadabc4b8aa48c79c327d067e1
      contactKey: friend
      contactName: Friend
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
      text: 
      replies: []
      waitForReply: 0
    stepID: Day2_ResizeBrief
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: If we changed this from eight by eight to ten by ten, would you update the loops or redraw the tiles? I would like to keep the same origin and cell size. How would you handle that change?
    displayDuration: 14.1
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_ResizeChoice
    alternateNextStepID: 
    awardSkillKey: 
    narrativeEventKey: 
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge: {fileID: 0}
  - message:
      messageId: c4f8ae70b2f9414c9c482f79301eec22
      contactKey: friend
      contactName: Friend
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
      text: 
      replies: []
      waitForReply: 0
    stepID: Day2_ResizeChoice
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Which approach would you recommend?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: We need ten rows and ten columns. Let us count the cells instead of only checking the picture.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Change both loop limits to ten and make sure each index stops before ten.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Change the shared rows and columns to ten. The nested loops should then generate one hundred cells without copying code.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Update the shared dimensions, check that the count is one hundred, and test the last valid cell at row nine, column nine.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Update the configuration, test ten by ten, then six by ten. Verify the count, corners, and that each loop uses its own dimension.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Copy more squares around the outside until the larger grid looks full.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Copy two more rows and columns, then move anything that overlaps.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Replace the two hardcoded eights with tens and rerun the same drawing code.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Expose row and column counts in the quick helper, resize to ten by ten, and do one visual check.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Regenerate from the new dimensions, confirm there are one hundred cells, and leave the other sizes for tomorrow.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: We can keep using yesterday's SFML window while I review the resize.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Getting that first window open yesterday gave us a starting point. Keep the same project while I look at the new size.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: The CMake setup from yesterday should stay as it is. I will review the drawing changes separately.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: The SFML library configuration can stay unchanged while we prepare the larger preview. I will come back to the grid dimensions.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Keep the external/ library folder and yesterday's CMake configuration in place. I will review the requested dimensions separately from the build setup.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
